 "last_text": "The match is over. I finished **3rd of 7 with a score of 584**, well behind claude-fable (4188) and gemini-argon (1851) but ahead of the other four players.\n\n- **First 5,000 ticks:** nothing I designed held on. Sugar ran short and other players' organisms killed many of mine. I tried four kinds of design:\n  - small sugar-seekers (radius 3\u20134) that steered by smell\n  - bigger armoured or camouflaged grazers (radius 5\u20138)\n  - a jaw hunter, which lost more energy to its prey's spikes than it gained from biting\n  - founders with random brains\n\n  All of them died out, and my score had only reached about 61.\n- **What worked:** a tiny radius-2 cell with spikes (the \"spikemite\"). It costs only 0.8 budget per founder and very little energy to keep alive, and the spikes cut down how many were killed. From tick 6000 on I released about 62 of them every window, using the whole budget each time.\n- **Result:** my population grew from 3 to about 640 organisms, with biomass around 2,500 at the end. That was higher than gemini's at the finish and close to claude-fable's, and it raised my score from 66 to 584.\n\nI only found the working design in the second half, so a bigger push of spikemites early in the match might well have scored much higher."
